SUMMARY:Postgres Conference 2027: Celebrating 20 Years of Community & Inno
 vation! 🐘🎉
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Postgres\nJoin us as Postgres Conference turns 20! We 
 are marking two decades of community-driven database excellence by gatheri
 ng developers\, DBAs\, architects\, and maintainers from around the globe 
 who build\, manage\, and scale Postgres in production.\n\n**📍 Venue:** 
 San Jose Marriott\, San Jose\, California\n📅 **Dates:** Apr 21\, 2027 
 – Apr 23\, 2027\n\n**Two Decades of Real-World Engineering**\nReaching t
 his milestone is a testament to the strength and resilience of open source
  engineering. Our community continues to push data systems forward\, from 
 core protocol advancements and a thriving extension ecosystem to autovacuu
 m tuning\, vector workloads\, high availability\, and data security.\n\n##
  **Interested in Speaking? 📢**\n\nHelp shape our 20th anniversary progr
 am! We invite practitioners\, researchers\, and community members to submi
 t speaker proposals. Share your hard-won production lessons\, architecture
  strategies\, security and compliance insights\, post-mortems\, or technic
 al benchmarks with our global audience.\n\n## **Conference Tracks**\n\nOur
  comprehensive\, multi-day\, multi-track program offers deep technical ses
 sions and holistic professional growth:\n\n* **Essentials:** Fundamental c
 oncepts\, best practices\, and foundational knowledge for new and growing 
 Postgres users\, including secure configuration and access control basics.
 .\n* **Dev:** Application design\, ORMs\, query optimization\, advanced SQ
 L features\, and secure coding practices such as preventing SQL injection 
 and using row-level security.\n* **Ops:** High availability\, replication\
 , backup & recovery\, performance tuning\, and infrastructure management\,
  along with hardening\, encryption\, auditing\, and compliance.\n* **Exten
 sions:** Extending Postgres functionality\, custom extension development\,
  and ecosystem integration\, plus security tooling like pgaudit and extens
 ion supply chain safety.\n* **AI:** Vector embeddings\, pgvector\, LLM int
 egration\, AI-driven data pipelines\, data sovereignty\, governance\, and 
 protecting sensitive data used in AI workloads.\n* **Professional Developm
 ent & Wellness:** Career growth\, engineering leadership\, mental health\,
  and maintaining work-life balance.\n* **Life & Fun:** Community stories\,
  creative technical pursuits\, and social networking activities.\n\n**How 
 to Submit Your Proposal**\nReady to share your knowledge with the Postgres
  community? Submit your proposal at [https://postgresconf.org/conferences/
 2027/program/proposals/new](https://postgresconf.org/conferences/2027/prog
 ram/proposals/new)\n\n**Visit the official conference portal to learn more
  about Postgres Conference 2027:**\n**👉 [https://postgresconf.org/confe
 rences/2027 ](https://postgresconf.org/conferences/2027)**\n\n**Questions?
 **\nReach out via [organizers@postgresconf.org](mailto:organizers@postgres
 conf.org) with any general questions or guidance regarding your proposal.\
 n\n**Interested in Sponsoring?**\nVisit the sponsorship page at [https://p
 ostgresconf.org/conferences/2027/sponsorships](https://postgresconf.org/co
 nferences/2027/sponsorships)
